{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL090aGVyc19MYW5ndWFnZS9GcmVuY2gtTGFuZ3VhZ2UvUm8lMjBHbyUyMFBhJTIwRyUyMCUyODE5NjMlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Ro Go Pa G","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/AjZgOidGeYN6ZGDHlwx1RZ9UFXV.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/olvFHqjMCCUVJ6NxxDxNJKPSl21.jpg","description":"Four short films by four different directors dealing with the principles of modern life. \"Illibatezza\" (Rossellini): The hostess Anna Maria, to dissuade an aggressive suitor who prefers maternal tendencies, assumes an unscrupulous attitude, obeying the suggestions of her distant boyfriend. \"The New World\" (Godard): The deflagration of an atomic bomb causes strange effects on the inhabitants of a city. \"La ricotta\" (Pasolini): During the filming of a film about a religious subject, the extra Stracci dies hanging on the cross due to an indigestion of ricotta. \"Il pollo spante\" (Gregoretti): While an expert illustrates to a board of merchants the most modern techniques to increase sales through the discovery of the secret self of the average consumer, the human story of a bourgeois who, following these suggestions, focuses on the purchase of a plot of land in the countryside.\n\nReleased 19 Feb 1963 · France, Italy · Language: Italian · 122 min\nStudio: Arco Film, Cineriz, Societé Cinématographique Lyre\n\nOn your server — Audio: Italian","releaseInfo":"1963","genres":["Comedy","Drama","Others"],"imdbRating":"7.2","imdb_id":"tt0056171","moviedb_id":59045,"tmdbId":59045,"runtime":"122 min","cast":["Rosanna Schiaffino","Bruce Balaban","Maria Pia Schiaffino","Jean-Marc Bory","Alexandra Stewart","Orson Welles","Mario Cipriani","Laura Betti"],"director":["Roberto Rossellini","Jean-Luc Godard"],"writer":["Roberto Rossellini","Jean-Luc Godard","Pier Paolo Pasolini"],"released":"1963-02-19T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Gay Beginnings of the End of the World.","country":"France, Italy","language":"Italian","app_extras":{"cast